From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: keep the eMMC at mmc1 when the board tree aliases it mmc2

A board's device tree may alias its eMMC controller by its own number,
mmc2 = &mmc2, as Allwinner's vendor trees do. U-Boot takes the first
alias that names a node, so that one wins over the mmc1 alias
sunxi-u-boot.dtsi adds, and the eMMC becomes mmc device 2. The sunxi
board code and the mmc_auto boot target assume device 1: booted from
the eMMC, mmc_bootdev is 1, "mmc dev 1" finds nothing, and the board
does not boot.

Drop the board's mmc2 alias where U-Boot gives the eMMC its own.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/sunxi-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/sunxi-u-boot.dtsi
index e1a9a7f5..56b16a49 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/sunxi-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/sunxi-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -10,6 +10,8 @@
 	aliases {
 		mmc0 = &mmc0;
 #if CONFIG_MMC_SUNXI_SLOT_EXTRA == 2
+		/* a board tree's mmc2 alias would come first and renumber it */
+		/delete-property/ mmc2;
 		mmc1 = &mmc2;
 #endif
 	};
